  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/Definition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> "Why two and fifteen degrees of freedom? Group contrasts and within-group residuals obey different fitted-mean constraints."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/Definition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> "How do sums of squares become comparable? Divide each by its own degrees of freedom; do not add the resulting mean squares."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-definition-11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
