  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-02> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **y_ij**: Recovery of preparation j in method i, in percent.
- **i and j**: i identifies method A, B or C. j numbers the six independent preparations within a method.
- **x̄_i**: Arithmetic mean recovery for method i, in percent. The bar marks an average. A, B and C identify the reported method means.
- **n_i**: Number of independent preparations in method i. It is 6 for each method.
- **Σ with j = 1 to n_i**: Add the recoveries for all preparations within method i. The factor 1/n_i divides that sum by the number of preparations.
- **=, comma and %**: Equality, separation of the reported quantities, and the unit percent recovery.

The formula describes the original synthetic river-water preparations."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-03> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **i, j; n**: Compared methods and their sample sizes.
- **ȳ; s²; sₚ²**: Mean recovery (%), sample and pooled variances (percentage points squared). **sₚ** is the pooled standard deviation.
- **ν; tᵢⱼ; Tν**: Degrees of freedom, observed standardized difference, and Student t under equal means. **Pr** is the tail probability. Absolute bars and doubling give both tails.
- **p; p adj; m**: Raw p-value, adjusted p-value, and number of planned pairs. The minimum caps the adjusted value at 1.

Here each pair uses six preparations per method and ten degrees of freedom."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-04> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **H_0; H_1**: Null and alternative hypotheses; subscripts zero and one label hypotheses, not groups.
- **μ_i; A; B; C**: Population mean recovery for group i, in percent; A, B and C are the method levels.
- **=; colon; semicolon**: Equality; introduces a hypothesis statement; separates the two hypotheses.
- **not all**: At least one pair of population means differs; it does not mean every pair differs.

Classical inference uses independent Normal errors with a common positive variance. ANOVA tests population means; it does not test the variance-equality assumption itself."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-05> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-05> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **y_ij**: Observed recovery of independent preparation j in method group i, in percent.
- **i; j**: Group index i runs from 1 to k; preparation index j runs from 1 to n_i within its group. A, B and C name the three methods.

The response is recovery in percent. Index j identifies a preparation within a group, not a time point or a pairing across methods. There are six independent preparations in each of the three original river-water groups."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-08> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-08> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **y_ij**: Observed recovery of independent preparation j in method group i, in percent.
- **i; j**: Group index i runs from 1 to k; preparation index j runs from 1 to n_i within its group. A, B and C name the three methods.
- **x̄_i; x̄**: Sample mean in group i and grand sample mean over all observations, both in percent. The grand mean weights each group mean by its group size.
- **n_i; N; k**: Number of independent preparations in group i, total number of preparations, and number of groups. N is the sum of the n_i.
- **−; +; =; parentheses**: Subtraction, addition, equality and grouping of operations. Signed departures are differences in percentage points.

These are the original synthetic river-water data, with three groups and six independent preparations per group. Recovery is recorded in percent, not as a fraction. A difference of percentage values is in percentage points. Algebraic decomposition does not require Normal errors; classical F calibration additionally requires independent Normal errors with a common positive variance."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-09> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-09> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **y_ij**: Observed recovery of independent preparation j in method group i, in percent.
- **i; j**: Group index i runs from 1 to k; preparation index j runs from 1 to n_i within its group. A, B and C name the three methods.
- **x̄_i; x̄**: Sample mean in group i and grand sample mean over all observations, both in percent. The grand mean weights each group mean by its group size.
- **n_i; N; k**: Number of independent preparations in group i, total number of preparations, and number of groups. N is the sum of the n_i.
- **SS_T; SS_B; SS_W**: Total, group-size-weighted between-group, and within-group sums of squared departures, in percentage points squared.
- **Σ_i; Σ_j**: Sum over all groups i from 1 to k, and all independent preparations j from 1 to n_i in that group.
- **−; +; =; parentheses**: Subtraction, addition, equality and grouping of operations. Signed departures are differences in percentage points.
- **superscript 2; juxtaposition**: Square the entire parenthesized departure; adjacent factors are multiplied. Squared departures have units of percentage points squared.
- **T; B; W**: Subscripts label total, between-group and within-group quantities.
- **leading 2; 0**: Two is the coefficient of the mixed term when a squared sum is expanded. Zero is the exact centered residual sum within each group, not an assumption about the population mean.

These are the original synthetic river-water data, with three groups and six independent preparations per group. Recovery is recorded in percent, not as a fraction. A difference of percentage values is in percentage points. Algebraic decomposition does not require Normal errors; classical F calibration additionally requires independent Normal errors with a common positive variance. Within each group, summing observed recovery minus its fitted group mean gives zero. Each group-mean departure is constant within that inner sum, which makes the summed mixed term zero."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-10> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **n_i; N; k**: Number of independent preparations in group i, total number of preparations, and number of groups. N is the sum of the n_i.
- **ν_T; ν_B; ν_W**: Total, between-group and within-group degrees of freedom; dimensionless counts of independently varying departures.
- **i; Σ from i=1 to k**: Group index and summation over all k groups.
- **−; =; parentheses; comma**: Subtraction, equality, grouping and separation of simultaneous identities.
- **1; 17; 2; 15**: One estimated mean consumes one degree of freedom. The remaining numbers are the original design’s total, between and within degrees of freedom.

Original synthetic river-water design: N is eighteen, k is three, and each n_i is six. The total degrees of freedom equal the between plus within degrees of freedom. This counting is algebraic; F calibration needs the additional error-model assumptions."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/DefinitionListEntry> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-11> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Symbols, units and conventions"@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/body> """- **n_i; N; k**: Number of independent preparations in group i, total number of preparations, and number of groups. N is the sum of the n_i.
- **SS_T; SS_B; SS_W**: Total, group-size-weighted between-group, and within-group sums of squared departures, in percentage points squared.
- **MS_B; MS_W**: Between-group and within-group mean squares, in percentage points squared.
- **B; W**: Subscripts meaning between groups and within groups.
- **−; =; fraction bar; comma**: Subtraction, equality, division, and separation of two reported calculations.
- **1; 42; 2**: One fitted grand-mean constraint; original between-group mean square 42 and original within-group mean square 2.

These are the original synthetic river-water data, with three groups and six independent preparations per group. Recovery is recorded in percent, not as a fraction. A difference of percentage values is in percentage points. Algebraic decomposition does not require Normal errors; classical F calibration additionally requires independent Normal errors with a common positive variance. Both divisors are positive. The within-group mean square pools residual variation under the common-variance model; the two mean squares are not additive."""@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-symbols-11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
